					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mickeyten" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4444390); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4444390&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200798" alt="mickeyten" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4444390)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mickeyten" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4444390); return false;" >mickeyten</a></span> <span class="odate time_1541456676 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">05 Nov 2018 22:24</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4050840">
									

<p>I want to upvote this <em>so badly</em> simply because it's skippified Lovecraft, but it's just&#8230; skippified Lovecraft, which makes it more literal and mundane than anything Lovecraft (or SCP, ideally) should be. It's well-written, don't get me wrong, and a loving tribute, but I was just hoping for a twist or something &quot;more&quot; that never happened. Honestly, there's nothing here that I couldn't get from reading Lovecraft's stories, which isn't good for an article directed at those familiar with them.</p>
<p>Side note, the list of instances with their &quot;capabilities&quot; kinda feels (to me, anyway) like something out of a roleplaying game rather than an SCP document. Maybe just replacing the word &quot;capabilities&quot; with &quot;notes&quot; may help?</p>

							</div>

								
