<p>Lovecraft described his creatures as indifferent. They view us the way we view ants. Their existence is a threat to humanity not because they are malevolent, but because they are so incomprehensible that simply looking at them can drive a person insane. In this article, not only are they malevolent, they're actively toying with Lovecraft and the people around him for entertainment.</p>
